      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so my company just sent me this new high-end ergonomic chair for my home office setup but i have a really bad feeling about it. i was looking at the specs and the mesh/fabric pattern looks way too consistent like there are sub-surface sensors or something. it feels like it's trying to track my vitals or how much i'm actually working. is there any way to mask my physical presence or body signals while sitting in it so they cant get a reading?",
